chat.json: a format-1 plaintext store (mimid-agent-jmap persist.rs), the
account "bob" (mimi://a.example/u/bob), written by mimid-agent-jmap itself
during a test run. Not hand-written or edited.

Source:    mimid, commit eaebf92 ("refactor(agent-store): move the
           stateless plaintext pieces out of agent-jmap"). Its persist.rs
           differs from e4e91cd only in one import path.
Generator: generate.rs in this directory (SHA-256
           8f20f48691e1da76bc6d37b8d208a41dcab0d2ad3a783a9a3b42c1df48b874f2),
           the test generate_chat_v1. It is a copy of the harness of
           crates/mimid-agent-jmap/tests/two_accounts.rs and runs
           a_restart_keeps_chats_and_messages with alice, bob and carol on
           one in-process mimid server. It adds: alice edits "before" and
           sends and retracts "gone soon"; bob sends "from bob", names
           alice "Alice A." and moves his ReadPosition; alice makes bob an
           admin and bans carol, which bob mirrors; alice sends "file.txt"
           with an attachment whose first fetch answers 503, so it waits
           for a retry. bob's chat.json is copied out at the end.
Command:   in a clean checkout of eaebf92 (git worktree add --detach),
             cp crates/mimid-agent-store/tests/fixtures/chat-v1/generate.rs \
                crates/mimid-agent-jmap/tests/generate_chat_v1.rs
             MIMID_CHAT_V1_OUT=<this directory>/chat.json \
               cargo test -p mimid-agent-jmap --test generate_chat_v1 \
               -- --ignored --nocapture
           then the checkout was removed. Run on 2026-11-20, Linux,
           stable Rust.
SHA-256:   chat.json 3a19e91c36c62f7d43216482022afed0f654413e8572927843947dab4f660303

The ids, times, keys and the server port differ on every run; the tests
read them from the file and do not depend on their values. The attachment
key in pending_attachments is a test key for test content.
